#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:6
msgid "Best practices for linking to your documentation"
msgstr "链接到文档的最佳实践"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:8
msgid ""
"Once you start to publish documentation, external sources will inevitably "
"link to specific pages in your documentation."
msgstr "一旦开始发布文档，外部来源必然会链接到你文档中的特定页面。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:11
msgid ""
"Sources of incoming links vary greatly depending on the type of "
"documentation project that is published. They can include everything from "
"old emails to GitHub issues, wiki articles, software comments, PDF "
"publications, or StackOverflow answers. Most of these incoming sources are "
"not in your control."
msgstr ""
"入站链接的来源因文档项目类型而差异巨大，可能包括旧邮件、GitHub Issue、wiki 文章、软件注释、PDF出版物或 StackOverflow "
"答案。这些入站来源大多不在你的控制范围内。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:15
msgid ""
"Read the Docs makes it easier to create and manage incoming links by "
"redirecting certain URLs automatically and giving you access to define your "
"own redirects."
msgstr "Read the Docs 通过自动重定向特定 URL 并允许你定义自己的重定向，让创建和管理入站链接更轻松。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:18
msgid ""
"In this article, we explain how our built-in redirects work and what we "
"consider \"best practice\" for managing incoming links."
msgstr "本文讲解内置重定向的工作原理，以及我们认为管理入站链接的\"最佳实践\"。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:23
msgid ":doc:`/versions`"
msgstr ":doc:`/versions`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:24
msgid "Read more about how to handle versioned documentation and URL structures."
msgstr "进一步了解如何处理版本化文档和 URL 结构。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:26
msgid ":doc:`/user-defined-redirects`"
msgstr ":doc:`/user-defined-redirects`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:27
msgid ""
"Overview of all the redirect features available on Read the Docs. Many of "
"the redirect features are useful either for building external links or "
"handling requests to old URLs."
msgstr "概述 Read the Docs 上所有可用的重定向功能。许多重定向功能既可用于构建外部链接，也可用于处理指向旧 URL 的请求。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:30
msgid ":doc:`/guides/redirects`"
msgstr ":doc:`/guides/redirects`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:31
msgid ""
"How to add a user-defined redirect, step-by-step. Useful if your content "
"changes location!"
msgstr "如何分步添加用户自定义重定向。当你的内容位置变更时很有用！"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:36
msgid "Best practice: \"permalink\" your pages"
msgstr "最佳实践：为页面设置\"永久链接\""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:38
msgid ""
"You might be familiar with the concept of `permalinks`_ from blogging. The "
"idea is that a blog post receives a unique link as soon as it's published "
"and that the link does not change afterward. Incoming sources can reference "
"the blog post even though the blog changes structure or the post title "
"changes."
msgstr ""
"你可能熟悉博客中的 `permalinks`_ "
"概念。其思路是博文一经发布即获得唯一链接，此后不再改变。即使博客结构变化或文章标题改动，外部来源仍可引用该博文。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:42
msgid ""
"When creating an external link to a specific documentation page, chances are"
" that the page is moved as the documentation changes over time."
msgstr "创建指向特定文档页面的外部链接时，随着文档演进，该页面很可能被移动。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:45
msgid ""
"How should a permalink look for a documentation project? Firstly, you should"
" know that a *permalink* does not really exist in documentation but it is "
"the result of careful actions to avoid breaking incoming links."
msgstr "文档项目的永久链接应是什么样：首先要知道，文档中并不真正存在*永久链接* ，它是通过谨慎操作避免破坏入站链接的结果。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:48
msgid ""
"As a documentation owner, you most likely want users clicking on incoming "
"links to see the latest version of the page."
msgstr "作为文档所有者，你多半希望点击入站链接的用户看到页面的最新版本。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:54
msgid "Good practice ✅"
msgstr "良好实践 ✅"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:56
msgid ""
"Use :ref:`page redirects <user-defined-redirects:Page redirects>` if you are"
" linking to the page in the :term:`default version` of the default language."
" This allows links to continue working even if those defaults change."
msgstr ""
"若链接指向默认语言的 :term:`default version` 中的页面，请使用 :ref:`页面重定向 <user-defined-"
"redirects:Page redirects>` 。这样即使这些默认值变化，链接仍能继续工作。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:57
msgid ""
"If you move a page that likely has incoming references, :doc:`create a "
"custom redirect rule </guides/redirects>`."
msgstr "若移动了可能存在入站引用的页面，请 :doc:`创建自定义重定向规则 </guides/redirects>` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:58
msgid ""
"Links to other Sphinx projects should use :doc:`intersphinx "
"</guides/intersphinx>`."
msgstr "指向其他 Sphinx 项目的链接应使用 :doc:`intersphinx </guides/intersphinx>` 。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:59
msgid "Use minimal filenames that don't require renaming often."
msgstr "使用简短的文件名，减少重命名需求。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:60
msgid ""
"When possible, keep original file names rather than going for low-impact URL"
" renaming. Renaming an article's title is great for the reader and great for"
" SEO, but this does not have to involve the URL."
msgstr "在可能的情况下保留原文件名，而非做影响较小的 URL 重命名。修改文章标题对读者和 SEO 都有益，但这不必涉及 URL。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:64
msgid ""
"Establish your understanding of the *latest* and :term:`default version` of "
"your documentation at the beginning. Changing their meaning is disruptive to"
" incoming links."
msgstr "在开始时就明确你文档中 *latest* 和 :term:`default version` 的含义。改变其含义会对入站链接造成破坏。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:65
msgid ""
"Keep development versions :ref:`hidden <versions:Version states>` so people "
"do not find them on search engines by mistake. This is the best way to "
"ensure that nobody links to URLs that are intended for development purposes."
msgstr ""
"保持开发版本 :ref:`隐藏 <versions:Version states>` ，避免人们误在搜索引擎中找到它们。这是确保没人链接到开发用途 "
"URL 的最佳方式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:67
msgid ""
"Use a :ref:`version warning notifications <versions:Version warning "
"notifications>` to ensure the reader is aware in case they are reading an "
"old (archived) version."
msgstr "使用 :ref:`版本警告通知 <versions:Version warning notifications>` ，确保读者在阅读旧（归档）版本时知情。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:71
msgid "Using Sphinx?"
msgstr "使用 Sphinx？"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:72
msgid ""
"If you are using ``:ref:`` for :doc:`cross-referencing </guides/cross-"
"referencing-with-sphinx>`, you may add as many reference labels to a "
"headline as you need, keeping old reference labels. This will make "
"refactoring documentation easier and avoid that external projects "
"referencing your documentation through :doc:`intersphinx "
"</guides/intersphinx>` break."
msgstr ""
"若你使用 ``:ref:`` 做 :doc:`交叉引用 </guides/cross-referencing-with-sphinx>` "
"，可在标题上按需添加多个引用标签，同时保留旧引用标签。这样重构文档更容易，也能避免通过 :doc:`intersphinx "
"</guides/intersphinx>` 引用你文档的外部项目失效。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:77
msgid "Questionable practice 🟡"
msgstr "存疑实践 🟡"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:79
msgid ""
"Avoid using specific versions in links unless users need that exact version."
" Versions get outdated."
msgstr "除非用户确实需要特定版本，否则避免在链接中使用具体版本。版本会过时。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:81
msgid ""
"Avoid using a public ``latest`` for development versions and do not make "
"your *default version* a development branch. Publishing development branches"
" can mean that users are reading instructions for unreleased software or "
"draft documentation."
msgstr "避免为开发版本使用公开的 ``latest`` ，也不要把*默认版本* 设为开发分支。发布开发分支可能导致用户阅读到未发布软件或草稿文档的说明。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:86
msgid "404 pages are also okay!"
msgstr "404 页面也可以接受！"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:87
msgid ""
"If documentation pages have been removed or moved, it can make the "
"maintainer of the referring website aware that they need to update their "
"link. Users will be aware that the documentation **project** still exists "
"but has changed."
msgstr "若文档页面被删除或移动，这可以让引用方网站的维护者意识到需要更新链接。用户也会知道文档**项目** 仍然存在，只是发生了变化。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/best-practice/links.rst:91
msgid ""
"The default Read the Docs 404 page is designed to be helpful, but you can "
"also design your own, see :doc:`/reference/404-not-found`."
msgstr ""
"Read the Docs 默认的 404 页面设计得较为有帮助，你也可以设计自己的页面，参见 :doc:`/reference/404-not-"
"found` 。"

